To ensure that your touch screen features are compatible across different iOS devices, you should use Auto Layout to design your user interface. Auto Layout allows you to create a flexible layout that can adapt to different screen sizes and orientations.
Here's an example of how to use Auto Layout to create a responsive user interface:
```
let button = UIButton()
button.translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false
button.setTitle("Tap me", for: .normal)
