 {'from': 'gpt', 'value': 'The Riemann Hypothesis is one of the most famous unsolved problems in mathematics. It concerns the distribution of prime numbers and their relationship to the zeros of the Riemann zeta function. More specifically, it suggests that all non-trivial zeros of the zeta function lie on a certain line in the complex plane. If this hypothesis were proven to be true, it would have profound consequences for number theory and other areas of mathematics.'}
