 {'from': 'gpt', 'value': 'Conditional probability is the probability of an event occurring given that another event has already occurred. It is denoted P(A|B), where A and B are events, and is defined as the probability of A occurring given that B has already occurred. For example, the probability of rolling a 6 on a fair die given that the roll is even would be a conditional probability.'}
 {'from': 'human', 'value': 'What is the difference between a vector and a scalar?'}
 {'from': 'gpt', 'value': 'A scalar is a quantity that only has magnitude, such as time or temperature. A vector, on the other hand, has both magnitude and direction, such as velocity or force. Vectors are typically represented graphically using arrows, with the length of the arrow representing the magnitude of the vector and the direction of the arrow indicating the direction of the vector. Scalars, on the other hand, are typically represented using a single number or variable.'}]

