 {'from': 'human', 'value': "I have a FastAPI application with a readme.md, main.py, and requirements.txt files. I need to refactor this application to use Flask instead of FastAPI. The readme.md should be updated to reflect the change in the framework, the main.py should be modified to use Flask's routing and request handling, and the requirements.txt should include Flask and its extensions. Specifically, the readme.md will be changed from stating 'This is a FastAPI app that provides some basic math functions.' to 'This is a Flask app that provides some basic math functions.' Additionally, the instructions for starting the app will be updated from 'Start the app by running `uvicorn main:app --reload`.' to 'Start the app by running `flask run`.' The Swagger UI documentation URL will also be updated to reflect the default Flask port, changing from 'http://localhost:8000/docs' to 'http://localhost:5000/docs'. The curl command in the readme.md will be modified to use the Flask default port by changing the endpoint from 'http://localhost:8000/calculate' to 'http://localhost:5000/calculate'. In the main.py file, the FastAPI specific imports and app initialization will be replaced with Flask equivalents, changing from 'from fastapi import FastAPI' and 'app = FastAPI()' to 'from flask import Flask, request, jsonify' and 'app = Flask(__name__)'. The route decorator will be updated from '@app.post('/calculate')' to '@app.route('/calculate', methods=['POST'])', and the request handling will be modified to use Flask's 'request.get_json()' method instead of FastAPI's dependency injection. The response will be changed from returning a dictionary to using Flask's 'jsonify' method. Lastly, the requirements.txt will be refactored to remove 'fastapi', 'uvicorn', and 'pydantic' and instead include 'flask' and 'flask-cors'."}
 {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '{"diff": "--- readme.md\n+++ readme.md\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n # FastAPI App\n\n-This is a FastAPI app that provides some basic math functions.\n+This is a Flask app that provides some basic math functions.\n\n ## Usage\n\n To use this app, follow the instructions below:\n\n 1. Install the required dependencies by running `pip install -r requirements.txt`.\n-2. Start the app by running `uvicorn main:app --reload`.\n+2. Start the app by running `flask run`.\n 3. Open your browser and navigate to `http://localhost:5000/docs` to access the Swagger UI documentation.\n\n ## Example\n\n To perform a basic math operation, you can use the following curl command:\n\n ```bash\n-curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"operation\": \"add\", \"operands\": [2, 3]}' http://localhost:8000/calculate\n+curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"operation\": \"add\", \"operands\": [2, 3]}' http://localhost:5000/calculate\n ```\n\n--- main.py\n+++ main.py\n@@ -1,29 +1,29 @@\n-from fastapi import FastAPI\n-from pydantic import BaseModel\n+from flask import Flask, request, jsonify\n\n-app = FastAPI()\n+app = Flask(__name__)\n\n\n-class Operation(BaseModel):\n-    operation: str\n-    operands: list\n+@app.route('/calculate', methods=['POST'])\n+def calculate():\n+    data = request.get_json()\n+    operation = data.get('operation')\n+    operands = data.get('operands')\n\n\n-@app.post('/calculate')\n-async def calculate(operation: Operation):\n-    if operation.operation == 'add':\n-        result = sum(operation.operands)\n-    elif operation.operation == 'subtract':\n-        result = operation.operands[0] - sum(operation.operands[1:])\n-    elif operation.operation == 'multiply':\n+    if operation == 'add':\n+        result = sum(operands)\n+    elif operation == 'subtract':\n+        result = operands[0] - sum(operands[1:])\n+    elif operation == 'multiply':\n         result = 1\n-        for operand in operation.operands:\n+        for operand in operands:\n             result *= operand\n-    elif operation.operation == 'divide':\n-        result = operation.operands[0]\n-        for operand in operation.operands[1:]:\n+    elif operation == 'divide':\n+        result = operands[0]\n+        for operand in operands[1:]:\n             result /= operand\n         else:\n             result = None\n-    return {'result': result}\n+    return jsonify({'result': result})\n\n--- requirements.txt\n+++ requirements.txt\n@@ -1,3 +1,2 @@\n-fastapi\n-uvicorn\n-pydantic\n+flask\n+flask-cors"}'}]

