The `quickSelect` function is based on the quickselect algorithm, which is a variation of the quicksort algorithm. The expected time complexity of quickselect is O(n), but the worst-case time complexity is O(n^2). However, since we randomly select the pivot element, the probability of worst-case performance is very low. By calling `quickSelect` on the flattened matrix, the `findKthSmallest` function performs k comparisons between the matrix elements. The time complexity of `quickSelect` is O(n log n) in the worst case, so the overall time complexity of `findKthSmallest` is O(mn log mn), which is O(n log n) if we assume that m and n are roughly equal."}
